Use case: production material artwork for a real-time 3D planet sphere.
Asset type: seamless 2:1 equirectangular albedo/surface-color map, high-resolution landscape (ideally 2048 x 1024), filling the entire rectangular frame edge to edge.
Reference use: use the supplied ORIGINAL A image only to match the central dark planet's surface character, antique engraving style, and restrained palette. Ignore the page layout, typography, orbit graphics, surrounding planets, and the sphere's lighting and shape. Create a material map, not a screenshot or projection of the reference.
Surface: richly irregular lunar geology with overlapping shallow craters, broken rims, naturally eroded pits, fractured mineral outcrops, and fine antique etched ivory/stone scuffs in dark rock. Vary crater sizes and density markedly: let rough cratered provinces fade into broad quiet dark plains, then into craggy fractured terrain. Keep the pale marks fine, restrained, and embedded within navy rock. Make detail dense at several scales but regionally uneven and natural, like the engraved surface of an old astronomical atlas. Avoid starburst craters, uniform fields of round marks, stippling, camouflage, chunky dots, repeated islands, grids, and broad web-like networks.
Palette: predominantly deep ink/navy and charcoal slate, in the spirit of #1b2939 through #303947, with small quantities of warm aged ivory, stone, and muted mineral gray. Keep most of the map dark; use pale engraving sparingly as local scuffs and fine fractured veins. No saturated blue, bright orange, or unrelated colors.
Mapping and lighting: a genuine full-surface equirectangular projection designed to wrap onto a sphere. Make the left and right edges meet seamlessly. Keep the upper and lower edge regions naturally calm and pole-compatible, with no stretched ridges, horizontal striation, bright border, or repeated latitudinal bands. Use neutral, even material lighting: no terminator, directional light, center glow, baked shading, cast shadow, rim light, vignette, or halo. The 3D scene supplies upper-left illumination.
Constraints: no sphere or circle silhouette, no background, orbit lines, stars, moons, labels, text, UI, border, or empty margin. Maintain continuous surface color and geology to all four edges. The result must read as a dark, intricately etched and craggy lunar material at ordinary display size.
